digest x86_64-windows "effects alloc sync irreversible(emit, actuate, erase, spend) | authority device priv any | may-trap yes | may-not-terminate"
doc "aet72c3lrayg2h5qro4sketuwplj5ixjouedap67tktfu4tnapafywx" "Returns once the entries of the directory `path` are on disk, as renames into it leave them: on\nLinux and macOS by syncing the directory, and on Windows, whose file systems journal their\nentries in order, and NaN OS, whose kernel keeps its file systems, once it finds that `path`\nnames a directory."
